  "validation_domain": "Six independently guarded ARM target cases, 87 native loop iterations: initial stop, signed clocks and deadline equality, FIFO/null and size16/17/32/33/512 pool paths, SPI63/64/65 cadence and lazy singleton boundary. Five portable fixture cases compare native idle/SPI/FIFO/pending/node observations with actual CCL locks/containers/pools and real integrated deferred/router/SPI bodies. Additional typed rate/route/GEQ copies survive caller mutation; borrowed projections restore after success/throw, capacity exhaustion and slot reuse validated. Shared static deadline exercised across separate Handler instances.",
  "limitations": [
    "Portable Linux source port; original ordinary int/unsigned return declaration remains unresolved. Namespace/mangling match does not establish original layout, ARM32 ABI or hardware interoperability. Original setProperty remains pure; typed enqueue API is independent supporting work, not reconstructed original setProperty.",
    "Native shared signed64 static deadline is retained. Caller must serialize threadEntry across all instances; stop publication uses explicit acquire/release source-port atomics. Pinned Linux CCL clock is nanoseconds; direct integer conversion intentionally avoids floating provider conversion.",
    "Finite capacities are explicit supplied source-port choices, not historical pool cardinalities. semanticBytes1..512 only; invalid sizes are guarded rather than reproduced. CCL linked list owns links, slots own value snapshots and queue owns slot arrays. Bind/unbind/destruction requires consumer joined and bound state no longer in use.",
    "Production dispatch keeps main then queue locks through dispatch/recycle under Root correction linked in contract-correction.json. Sealed original contract is preserved. Native/Core implementation source was not reconstructed.",
    "Original native fixtures execute only the target and capture named Core/app imports; lazy SPI ctor is a captured native boundary. Portable replay uses prebound borrowed SPI with disabled receive state and zero pins, actual onIdle/router/deferred bodies, captured clock/sleep/ack and aborting device I/O. Default SPI lazy hardware construction is not exercised in portable replay.",
    "Portable runtime_error cleanup restores state, clears property and returns pool slot with no swallowed exceptions. Native exception unwinding and C++ cancellation forced-unwind execution are not tested; scope cleanup is an intentional source-port guarantee. No interleaving/hardware test. 32-bit loop wrap is defined by uint32 arithmetic but full wrap execution is outside bounded replay."
